+1.1 By [A1], each kernel and cokernel is finite-dimensional, so each top exterior power in the Definition is a one-dimensional complex vector space. Their tensor product and dual are therefore a one-dimensional Hermitian line with the specified Quillen metric. [given, A1, algebra]
+
+2.1 Parallel transport for a unitary connection is unitary, and the endpoint gauge identification is unitary by the chosen representation $R$. Their composite around $\gamma$ is thus a unitary automorphism of a one-dimensional complex line, hence multiplication by a unique scalar of modulus one. A change of unit vector in the fiber conjugates that scalar, which does not change it because $U(1)$ is abelian. Therefore $\operatorname{Hol}_{\gamma}(\mathcal L)$ is a well-defined element of $U(1)$. The further interpretation of this phase as the residual global part of a background anomaly is conditional on [F1]'s planned decomposition and is not established until its absent carrier is supplied. [given, F1, A1, L1, step 1.1, algebra] ∎
