+## Completed item: `pthm-aqft-global-anomaly-test`
+
+**Claim and conventions.** For one massless left-handed Weyl doublet of a nondynamical $SU(2)$ background symmetry on oriented, standard-spin Euclidean $S^4$, assume the exact chiral index input $\operatorname{ind}_{\mathbb C}D_A^+=1$. With anti-Hermitian curvature and $I_6=[\widehat A\operatorname{ch}(E)]_6$, the fundamental representation has zero local polynomial, while the order-two center loop has determinant/Pfaffian holonomy $-1$. For $N$ copies the sign is $(-1)^N$; the adopted five-dimensional mod-two-index response cancels this specified loop. A separate one-vertex $BC_2$ groupoid check shows why the boundary-only nontrivial character is not a scalar gauging weight and why the combined unit weight sums to $1/2$. This does not claim all anomalies vanish for even $N$, nor does it prove the source index input locally.
