+**Dependencies.** Direct: `def-aqft-thooft-anomaly` (formulation prerequisite, missing batch-41 carrier), `def-aqft-global-anomaly-holonomy` (same batch), `def-aqft-anomaly-inflow-relative-theory` (same batch), and `def-qftx-finite-groupoid-integration` (published local finite-groupoid mathematics supplier). Planned `dependency_level: 3`, one above the highest in-run item supplier at level 2. The required page edge to `qftx-finite-symmetry-gauging` is recorded separately and verified against its current batch-14 carriers. The index-one equality is an explicit hypothesis supported by the complete relevant Witten–Wang–Wen source argument; it is not a local index-theorem proof in this item.
+
+**Root mathematical context checked.** I read the current root `cor-spin-dirac-index-formula-with-arbitrary-twist` carrier and its direct geometric index theorem statement/proof. The corollary requires full AC and has a heat-kernel/Getzler proof through its current `thm-geometric-clifford-module-dirac-index-formula` dependency. The exact corollary, spinor definition, and geometric theorem are absent from this physics `math-imports.json` snapshot; the current external-reuse inventory records them as source/context rather than a canonical active edge. The relevant root proof chain is not claimed here as a local supplier. The theorem therefore keeps the index equality $\operatorname{ind}_{\mathbb C}D_A^+=1$ explicit in its hypothesis and source record. To turn that condition into a derived local-library result, Root must either authorize/pin the exact mathematical chain or place a complete mathematical supplier on an appropriate support page. No root math file or import receipt was edited.
+
