"},"statement":"Let $\\mathcal A_U^{g,p}$ be the finite-jet horizontal-form spaces on a smooth open set $U\\subseteq\\mathbb R^4$, with nilpotent BRST differential $s$, horizontal differential $d_H$, and $sd_H+d_Hs=0$. In bidegree $(1,4)$, define $H^{1,4}(s\\mid d_H)$ as the ghost-number-one four-forms $a_4$ satisfying $sa_4+d_Hb_3=0$ for some $b_3$, modulo the subspace $\\{sC_4+d_Hr_3:C_4\\in\\mathcal A_U^{0,4},\\ r_3\\in\\mathcal A_U^{1,3}\\}$. If a local counterterm changes an anomaly representative from $a_4$ to $a'_4=a_4+sC_4+d_Hr_3$, then $[a'_4]=[a_4]$ in $H^{1,4}(s\\mid d_H)$.","provenance":{"statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated"},"sources":{"references":[{"title":"Adel Bilal, Lectures on Anomalies (full lecture notes)","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/0802.0634","locator":"§§9.2 and 9.4, printed pp. 71–77: local BRST coboundaries, consistent anomaly representatives, and the local-counterterm ambiguity."},{"title":"Enrique Alvarez, Gauge Anomalies","url":"https://members.ift.uam-csic.es/ealvarez/anomalies.ea.pdf","locator":"§2.4, printed pp. 36–38: a local Bardeen–Zumino counterterm changes the consistent/covariant representative while preserving the underlying local anomaly data."}]},"library":"physics","proof_strategy":"direct"},{"id":"def-aqft-thooft-anomaly","kind":"definition","domain":"physics","title":"Local perturbative ’t Hooft anomaly modulo counterterms","reference":"items/def-aqft-thooft-anomaly.md","design_state":"Step 1 authored; current interface, source evidence, and readiness are recorded in batch-41 notes.","dependency_level":0,"deps":["def-aqft-p-form-global-symmetry","def-qftx-local-brst-cohomology"],"dependency_roles":{"def-aqft-p-form-global-symmetry":"formulation-prerequisite","def-qftx-local-brst-cohomology":"mathematical-premise"},"statement":"Fix a four-dimensional smooth spacetime region $U\\subseteq\\mathbb R^{1,3}$ with a stated orientation, spin structure, boundary conditions, and unit system. A selected model specifies a continuous global symmetry group $H$, its action on the fields and observables, the nondynamical background connections, the field and jet domains, a regulator and measure or formal perturbative generating functional, and the admissible local counterterms. A background connection is nondynamical model data: it transforms under local changes of background trivialization but is not integrated over.","provenance":{"statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable"},"sources":{"references":[{"title":"Adel Bilal, Lectures on Anomalies (full lecture notes)","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/0802.0634","locator":"§§4.1, 9.1–9.4, and 10.4, printed pp. 18–27 and 69–88: effective-action variation, consistent BRST descent, counterterm ambiguity, and the local/global scope boundary."},{"title":"Enrique Alvarez, Gauge Anomalies","url":"https://members.ift.uam-csic.es/ealvarez/anomalies.ea.pdf","locator":"§§2.1–2.4, printed pp. 25–38: the local BRST descent, representation-dependent polynomial, and counterterm changes between consistent and covariant representatives."}]},"library":"physics","proof_strategy":"definition","physical_scope":"A definition of the infinitesimal, local anomaly class of a specified background-coupled global symmetry in four dimensions; it asserts no global-anomaly classification, continuum QFT existence, or automatic gauging."},{"id":"def-aqft-anomaly-matching-data","kind":"definition","domain":"physics","title":"Flat-space chiral anomaly-matching data and regulator convention","reference":"items/def-aqft-anomaly-matching-data.md","design_state":"Step 1 authored; current interface, source evidence, and readiness are recorded in batch-41 notes.","dependency_level":1,"deps":["def-aqft-thooft-anomaly","def-aqft-p-form-global-symmetry","def-qftx-local-brst-cohomology","def-qftx-nonabelian-brst-complex","lem-qftx-nonabelian-brst-nilpotence","def-aqft-cubic-anomaly-polynomial"],"dependency_roles":{"def-aqft-thooft-anomaly":"formulation-prerequisite","def-aqft-p-form-g